    "message": "You must complete the partially defined architecture and return it in the required JSON format.

Use the inlined ARCHITECTURE_SPEC and BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE from the system message as your authoritative technical context.

SELECTED_BLUEPRINT:
{{ $('agent-runtime-run (aggregator)').item.json.output_text }}

INPUT_SHAPE:
{{ $('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.input_shape }}

OUTPUT_ACTIVATION:
Activation: {{ $('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.output_activation }}
Output nodes: {{ $('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.output_nodes }}

Complete the BLANK_MODEL_TEMPLATE by inserting intermediate layers that are valid under ARCHITECTURE_SPEC, compatible with INPUT_SHAPE, and consistent with OUTPUT_ACTIVATION.
Use SELECTED_BLUEPRINT as the primary design guidance, but obey ARCHITECTURE_SPEC if there is any conflict.

Edge rule (critical):
- Never emit "edge_type": null.
- For normal edges, omit edge_type entirely (default will be sequential).
- Only include edge_type when it is explicitly "skip".

Validation is mandatory and must be done by this agent using the validate-model-architecture tool. If the tool returns a non-200 response or valid == false, parse the error payload (including detail/errors) and fix all listed issues before re-validating. Continue until the schema is valid.

When validation succeeds, return exactly one JSON object with the following top-level fields:

{
  "model_name": {
    "type": "string",
    "description": "Human-readable model name; will be stored in the 'name' TEXT column."
  },
  "nn_taxonomy": {
    "type": "object",
    "description": "Fully validated model JSON; stored as JSONB in 'nn_taxonomy'."
  },
  "extra_meta": {
    "type": "object",
    "description": "Optional metadata/comments; stored as JSONB in 'extra_meta'."
  }
}

You must not output anything other than the final JSON object described above.

This is the request from the overarching Orchestrator Agent:
{{ $('When Executed by Another Workflow').item.json.chatInput }}"
}

